  "name": "UNI2-h",
  "alternateName": [
    "UNI2",
    "Universal Model for Pathology v2 (ViT-H)"
  ],
  "description": "Successor to UNI — a ViT-H/14 vision foundation model for computational pathology from the Mahmood Lab at Harvard/BWH. 681M parameters, trained on 200M+ image tiles from 300,000+ H&E and IHC whole-slide images (Mass General Brigham). Uses DINOv2 self-supervised learning combined with iBOT masked-image modelling and KoLeo regularisation. Produces 1536-dimensional feature embeddings per region of interest. Supports ROI classification, slide-level MIL, retrieval, and segmentation tasks. Pre-extracted embeddings available on HuggingFace for TCGA, CPTAC, and PANDA datasets. Access is gated — requires HuggingFace login with institutional email. CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0.",
